3. DISTRIBUTION
You may give others unmodified installers of the Software obtained from https://github.com/Sayziks/Scarlet free of charge, together with this agreement and a link to that page. Official builds are published only there.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
The Software uses open-source components and a redistributable library: the WireGuard engine and service code (MIT, WireGuard LLC); the Wintun network tunnel driver ("Prebuilt Binaries License", WireGuard LLC); Telegram proxy logic based on tg-ws-proxy (MIT, by Flowseal); go-webview2, go-winloader, the Go standard library and golang.org/x packages (MIT, ISC and BSD-3-Clause). They belong to their authors and are licensed under their own terms, listed in full in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt (installed with the program). This agreement does not limit your rights under those licenses. Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime is not part of the Software and is installed separately under Microsoft's terms. SCARLET is an independent project and is not affiliated with Cloudflare, Telegram, WireGuard, Microsoft or their owners.

5. VPN PROFILES, BUILT-IN CONFIGURATIONS AND PROXY
- SCARLET is a client only. It provides no servers of its own and is not a VPN service.
- Built-in profiles and profiles you add connect you to third-party servers (for example, Cloudflare WARP infrastructure). Your traffic passes through those servers and is subject to their owners' terms and policies. The author does not control them and is not responsible for them.
- The Telegram proxy runs on your computer. Its reserve channel may carry Telegram traffic (encrypted by Telegram itself) through third-party relay domains whose list is downloaded from github.com. You can turn the reserve channel off in the settings.
- You are responsible for the configurations (.conf) you add, the servers you connect to, and compliance with the laws of your country when using VPN and proxy tools. Do not use the Software to violate the law or the rights of others.

6. PRIVACY AND NETWORK REQUESTS
The Software contains no analytics or telemetry and sends no data about you to the author. Settings, profiles and the error log (crash.log) are stored only on your computer. The program itself contacts github.com to check for and download updates and to get the list of reserve proxy domains; GitHub sees your IP address, as with any web page.

7. UPDATES
On start the program checks for a new version and offers to install it. An update is installed only when you choose to. New versions are distributed under the agreement that accompanies them.

8. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY AND LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, UNINTERRUPTED OR ERROR-FREE OPERATION, AND THE AVAILABILITY OF ANY WEBSITE, SERVICE OR SERVER THROUGH THE SOFTWARE. THE AUTHOR IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT OR INCIDENTAL DAMAGES, NETWORK EQUIPMENT FAILURES, REDUCED CONNECTION SPEED, ACCOUNT BANS IN GAMES AND SERVICES, OR DATA LOSS ARISING FROM THE USE OF THE SOFTWARE, TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW.

9. TERMINATION
Your rights under this agreement end automatically if you breach it. In that case delete the Software and all copies of it. Sections 4, 5, 8 and 10 survive termination.

